Phase 0 safety change to the DDK sample — the only modification we make to it.

The sample's AEP_INITIALIZE calls Port_Set_IRQ_Handler, which registers
[edi].DDB_irq_number with VPICD. That number comes from the device node. Our probe
devnode declares no IRQ, so the field is zero — and virtualising IRQ 0 means the
system timer.

This machine has already lost a subsystem once to a driver touching an interrupt it
had no business touching (issue #22: the LS-120 miniport left IRQ 1 masked and killed
the keyboard). A probe is not worth that risk.

The line goes rather than being made conditional, because the XT-IDE card is jumpered
without an interrupt: the real driver polls, PORTISR.ASM is deleted in phase 1, and
the whole VPICD interaction disappears with it. This is a preview of that, not a
workaround.

Applied by build.ps1 to a working copy. The DDK sources themselves are not in this
repository and are not redistributable.

--- PORTAER.ASM	original
+++ PORTAER.ASM	phase 0
@@ -240,7 +240,10 @@
 	;
 	; now set the IRQ handler
 	;

-	call	Port_set_irq_handler
+; PHASE 0, this project: NOT the DDK original.
+; Registering DDB_irq_number (zero on a devnode with no IRQ) with VPICD would
+; virtualise the system timer. The XT-IDE card polls; see phase0-no-irq.patch.
+;	call	Port_set_irq_handler

 	;
 	; all set.  note that AEP_SUCCESS was preset by calling routine.
